<title>UK: Hays dips on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Hays dips on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hays Plc dipped on profit-taking, even as the broad market climbed to new records, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1114 GMT, the shares were down 7p to 556-1/2.</p>
<p>Dealers said they weren't aware of any specific factor that prompted the profit-taking.</p>
<p>One noted that there had been a steady buyer of the shares up until recently. The buyers absence in the market during the last couple of sessions, he said, may have sparked the profit-taking.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
